 overnight. Israel Mazin Founder & CEO Why You Should Watch AI is making digital impersonation faster, easier to execute, and dramatically more scalable. In this Techstrong TV interview, Israel explores how attackers are using AI and readily available scam kits to create convincing impersonation attacks at a scale that traditional approaches struggle to match. Key Highlights AI Has Changed the Scale of Impersonation Attackers can use AI to create and launch impersonation campaigns faster and at significantly greater scale, while lowering the technical barrier for less sophisticated fraudsters. The Next Frontier: Agent Impersonation As AI agents increasingly perform actions and transactions on behalf of people, fake agents and stolen agent identities introduce a new digital trust problem. Israel explores why protecting the authenticity of these interactions will become increasingly important. Fighting AI Scams and Agent Impersonation Automation, real-time signal correlation, and earlier visibility are increasingly important as organizations attempt to identify attacks, exposed users, and attacker activity before fraud occurs. What You'll Learn Watch the full Techstrong TV interview to hear Israel and Alan discuss how AI is reshaping digital impersonation, what organizations need to consider as attacks scale, and why agent impersonation could become the next major frontier for fraud prevention and digital trust. Solutions Overview Solution overview By use case Account takeover (ATO) Digital Impersonation Protection Credit card data theft By attack technique Man in the Middle (MitM) Remote desktop takeover Credential stuffing SEO poisoning By team For security teams For fraud & risk teams For Digital Business teams By industry Banking Credit Unions Airlines Retail & Ecommerce Hospitality Products Products Overview Technology Technology Overview Partnerships Partner Up Partner Portal Resources Library Frost & Sullivan Analysis of Memcyco Blog Get the latest insights Glo