nvestigations tell you what happened. The harder problem is seeing what happened before the fraud became visible. Memcyco is heading to Nashville for the 2026 IAFCI International Training Conference, joining financial-crime professionals from across the public and private sectors to compare what teams are seeing, where existing controls are losing visibility, and how modern scams are changing the investigation timeline. About the Event The IAFCI International Training Conference brings together the financial-crime investigation community for three days of practical learning and collaboration. The 2026 program combines expert keynotes, specialized financial-crime breakout tracks, workshops, panels, networking and technology showcases, with discussions focused on emerging threats and stronger collaboration across sectors. Turn fragmented signals into preemptive fraud protection Memcyco technology correlates attack signals in real time to identify exposed users, protect at-risk accounts, expose attackers and help teams disrupt impersonation and account takeover attacks before fraud occurs. Our Technology Meet Memcyco Fraud starts earlier than most investigations can see. We’re even earlier . Customers are increasingly targeted outside the environments organizations control, through impersonation, deceptive digital journeys and social engineering designed to manipulate them before a traditional security signal appears. Memcyco helps fraud and security teams gain visibility into that earlier stage. We’ll be discussing: Digital impersonation: identifying when customers encounter fraudulent versions of trusted brands. Scam intelligence: understanding attacks while customers are being targeted, not simply reconstructing them afterwards. Account takeover: connecting activity outside the login journey with the attacks that eventually reach customer accounts. Earlier fraud signals: giving teams more context before an incident turns into a case number. AI-enabled deception: addressing attacks that can now be created, personalised and scaled faster. The question we’re bringing to Nashville is simple: How much more could fraud teams stop if they could see the attack before the transaction? Where to find Memcyco during the event: Meet the Memcycans Our team on the ground brings hands-on experience across fraud prevention, digital risk, and customer protection, working directly with financial services, fintech, travel, and digital brands. If investigation is working, but visibility isn’t, that’s the gap we focus on. We should talk. Get in touch below for 1:1 discussions either before, during or after the event. Devin Sorin Business Development Representative White “in” Letters Inside A Solid Purple Circle, Resembling The LinkedIn Logo, Create A Modern And Professional Look—perfect For Representing Cybericon2024. Mail William Roberts Business Development Representative White “in” Letters Inside A Solid Purple Circle, Resembling The LinkedIn Logo, Create A Modern And Professional Look—perfect For Representing Cybericon2024. Mail What’s New? BLOG 23 Sep 2026 iGaming Fraud Prevention: How to Protect Player Accounts Preemptively Without Adding Friction View Article Podcasts 22 Sep 2026 Techstrong TV: Fighting AI Scams and Agent Impersonation Watch Podcasts 17 Sep 2026 The MemcycoFM Show: Ep 30 – How to Reduce Payment Fraud Risk Without Adding Customer Friction Watch BLOG 16 Sep 2026 Online Gambling Fraud: How Fake Sites, Apps and Social Ads Divert Player Deposits View Article BLOG 8 Sep 2026 How to Reduce Payment Fraud Risk Without Adding Customer Friction View Article Podcasts 31 Aug 2026 The MemcycoFM Show: Ep 29 – How to Identify Users Exposed to Brand Impersonation Attacks Watch BLOG 28 Aug 2026 Brand Impersonation Protection Software: What to Look For Beyond Domain Takedown View Article Podcasts 16 Aug 2026 The MemcycoFM Show: Ep 28 – AI Threat Intelligence vs. Traditional Threat Intelligence: A Practical Guide for CISOs Watch In the news 13 